planner_precedence
  # Plan 10 leaf 18 (issue #1138) — the route arms of the agentic planner
  # order, first match wins, exactly as they run in
  # src/agentic_coding/planner.rs. Precedence is behaviour, so it is named here
  # where an edit is reviewable; the planner joins this order to its coded arms
  # and asserts an exact permutation at every plan step, so a seed edit can
  # never silently drop, duplicate or reorder a route (the issue #663
  # handler-precedence join, applied to the agentic cascade).
  #
  # plan_chat_step_routes -- the delivery-peeling head of the cascade
  conversation_control_decline # a bare continuation cue with nothing to resume is answered by the conversation handler, never routed (issue 1095)
  computer_use # seed-defined computer-use plans own their exact multilingual prompts before broad write and search routing (issue 707)
  authoritative_literal_write # an explicit exact-content marker makes the following bytes authoritative, ahead of edit and source semantics (issue 708)
  program_contract # binds the semantic operands of a program before its source path is read as a destination; may reroute the composed command
  evidence_record # peels a named delivery off the request and re-plans the residual, so proof files are written before a change route answers (issue 1066)
  #
  # plan_settled_routes -- the settled tail of the cascade
  git_commit # a commit-only request is one shell step, claimed before search reads its file listing as a lookup (issue 1133)
  workspace_change # a learned workspace-change procedure owns grounded repository rewrites before source creation or shell routing
  generated_source # a source-code description is executable bytes, not literal file content; lower bounded seed-backed source tasks first
  structured_edit # a structured source edit is a read/derive/write transaction, ahead of the broad literal-write parser
  structured_document # a source-backed structured document is authored, not observed; ahead of the ordinary file reader (issue 1066)
  statement_audit # a repository audit names the artifact its CLI command will produce; replayable recipe ahead of literal fallback
  task_obligations # an enumerated request is planned one obligation at a time and finishes only when the ledger discharges every node (issues 1099, 1138)
  literal_write # resolves an unambiguous literal write before keyword recipes; arbitrary filenames may contain recipe words (issue 1066)
  algorithm_learning # portable event logs own the independently validated trace-learning route
  procedure # a freely phrased procedure is one compile, persist and verify recipe on both surfaces
  learning_report # specific self-inspection routes precede broad formalization; before self-healing on artifact scope
  code_artifact # workspace mutations are grounded in client-owned file bytes; after the learning recipes so their artifacts stay theirs
  self_heal # the self-healing recipe, checked ahead of formalization
  dreaming_audit # the dreaming-audit recipe, checked ahead of formalization
  self_ast # the self-AST census recipe, checked ahead of formalization
  source_links # its request legitimately names "links", which the broad formalization match would otherwise capture
  learning_ledger # the promotion step after an approved repair case; its request names "Links Notation"
  explain # the grounded self-explanation recipe; its request names "Links Notation" as the output format
  change_request # the user-initiated self-change recipe; its request names "Links Notation" as the output format
  repair_strategy # classifies an arbitrary failure trace into a grounded, human-gated strategy
  rebuild_plan # recompile-and-reattach after an accepted change; its keywords key on "reattach" (issue 558)
  google_trends_learning # before the sibling catalog recipe; both legitimately name "Google Trends"
  google_trends_catalog # the trends catalog recipe, behind its learning sibling
  question_catalog # enumerate every possible question smallest-first; its keywords are disjoint from the sibling recipes (issue 527)
  file_analysis # a request to inspect named files and report findings is a typed read plus audit, not an issue report (issue 1138 self-use)
  report_flow # the agent-mode counterpart of the report action of the web UI; a conversation state machine (issues 687, 822)
  conversation_recall # recall answers from earlier turns of the conversation before any route re-reads them
  follow_up_answer # a follow-up on a tool result is answered from that result, not re-planned
  contextual_reference_clarification # an ambiguous reference in context asks its clarification before any search
  definition_followup # a definition follow-up reuses the prior subject instead of searching for the sentence
  intent_edit # the edit step of the intent router, ahead of the typed read route that would misread an edit target
  typed_file_read # the established list/read recipe whenever the client exposes its typed read capability
  local_search # a meanings-driven explicit local scope dominates generic search verbs; widens only after emptiness
  comparison # a comparison request builds its table before the shell cascade can collapse it into one command
  named_capability_table # the decision table decides the seven named capabilities here, ahead of the shell lowering their rows declare as fallback (plan 10 leaf 11)
  shell_command # a resolved shell command runs through the file fallback, the mutating-action recipe, or one verified step
  file_read # any remaining file read request plans its typed read
  formalization_recipe # a formalization request renders its formalization before the remaining doc and research routes
  meaning_detail # a meaning-detail request answers from the lexicon before research
  diagram # a diagram request renders its diagram before research
  web_fetch # a typed URL object is more specific than broad research prose; fetch it before the research recipe (issue 1066)
  workspace_inspection # a request to look at the handed repository is answered by reading it, before research routers claim the question shape (issue 1066)
  task_structure # a question about how a task decomposes is answered by decomposing it, before research claims the question shape (issue 1066)
  capability_table_named_or_local # the named-or-local stage of the decision table, declined for requests already under way in a recipe (issue 781)
  positional_edit_decline # an instruction that edits a named file is never a web question; decline rather than search the sentence (issues 1115, 1133)
  web_research_query # the research recipe for an explicit query, ahead of the narrower search step of the intent router
  intent_web_search # the web search step of the intent router for a request the research query reader declined
  code_search_fallback # keeps grep available to grep-only clients without letting an earlier local tool steal a web request (issue 758)
  research_continuation # continues a recipe with results already in hand; unresolved queries resume before anything else claims the turn
  latest_turn_answer # a turn the latest tool result already answers is answered from that result
  note_composition # a document a request says a note must cover is composed only after nothing else claims its parts (issue 1066)
  general_change_fallback # the whole-request composer, after every route that could answer a named part outright
  web_research_final # the last research pass for an unresolved query the earlier readers declined
  capability_table_open_web # the open-web stage of the decision table, last — research routers own a bare term first (issue 745)
